==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s (4,000%) spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Duche]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Baa Baa]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 4~20 seconds<sup>120f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Gory Dark]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Doge]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**1 [[Youcan]] spawns.
**2 [[Baa Baa]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**3 [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**3 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn, delay 1~4 seconds<sup>30f~120f</sup>.
**3 [[Kory|Kories]] spawn, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage can be pretty difficult if you don't have any high range [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immune]] Ubers, as the Owlbrows deal very high damage per hit.

[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] proves extremely useful here, and can survive a hit from YouCan at level 46, although this is not necessary. Wave Immune meatshields such as talented [[Li'l Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Mohawk Cat]] or [[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Gold Cat]]'s True Form can help patch up holes in your defence.

Most Wave Immune attackers can be useful, such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]. Dancer Cat's [[Surge Attack]] Talent or [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Storm Beast Naala]] for {{2c}}+ can also help chip at the Owlbrows, although this is not necessary.

==Trivia==
*In Japan, there's a point system called "Bellmark", where organizations collect points from everyday products, which are then converted into funds to support schools and educational activities, with a portion of the funds also going towards educational assistance for students in need. Japanese students are encouraged to collect these points, hence the name, "Bell Collecter".

